      <div class="container area features">
        <h2 class="fw-bold pb-2 border-bottom">Career Path</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            Dennis started his career at the Kwame Nkrumah University of Science
            and Technology (KNUST-Ghana), where he gained foundational knowledge
            in electrical and electronic systems and design, completing with a
            Bachelor's degree First Class honors in Electrical and Electronic
            Engineering, 2018.
          </li>
          <li>
            Upon completion he had the noble opportunity of participating in the
            Huawei ICT Skills Competition (HAINA), designed to equip young
            engineers with skills in entreprise networks design and
            implementation while also showcasing their talents.
          </li>
          <li>
            He received the second best award at the regional contest of the
            HAINA competition with member participants from countries in the
            Sub-Saharian region.
          </li>
          <li>
            He further earned a nomimation for the Global Contest (HAINA) with
            participants from all major continents, held in China-2018,
            following his exemplary performance and dedication at the regional
            contest.
          </li>
          <li>
            His contribution and abilities was duly recognized with an
            Outstanding Performance Award at the global contest (HAINA) in
            China.
          </li>
          <li>
            Dennis later joined Huawei Tech. as a Systems Engineer (2018-2019),
            actively participating in entreprise networks feasibility studies,
            design, configuration and resource management for a number of
            wireless and core network projects.
          </li>
          <li>
            Later, he decided to pursue further studies at the Texas A&M
            University (Kingsville-US), completing with a Master's degree in
            Electrical Engineering, 2021. He specialized in electronic and
            embedded systems/design, wireless networks and signal processing.
          </li>
          <li>
            During and prior his graduate studies, he worked as an Intern with
            Intel Corp. where he was devoted to both electronic model and
            simulation methods development to aid the design of technology
            process nodes for next generation electronic products.
          </li>
          <li>
            He received a number of recognitions for his relentless efforts to
            technology design process at Intel Corp.
          </li>
          <li>
            His current focus intersects the areas of electronic prototyping, application development,
            database systems and machine learning (ML) models for networked systems.
          </li>
          <li>
            Dennis is a proponent of continuous learning and development: as the world continues to evolve the technology race remains intense and the need for global technocrats is upscale
          </li>
        </ul>
